# The UI kit is published to GitHub Packages, not the public registry, so this
# scope has to be pointed away from npmjs.org. Lives at the workspace root
# because that is where pnpm looks; a copy under frontend/ is ignored when
# install runs from here, which shows up as a confusing 404.
@coverland-engineering:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com

# The token deliberately is not here. pnpm refuses to expand environment
# variables in credentials read from a project .npmrc — the file is committed,
# so a line like `_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}` could be edited to point a real
# secret at an attacker's registry. Each developer sets it once, outside the
# repo:
#
#   pnpm config set "//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken" <token>
#
# The token needs only the read:packages scope, and must be a classic one —
# fine-grained tokens do not work against the npm registry yet.
